# gitleaks false-positive suppressions — CI support only (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml's `secret-scan` job and
# docs/handoff/008-ci-pipeline.md).
#
# Every line below is a specific finding (path:rule:line), verified by hand
# on 2026-09-08 to be a cryptographic algorithm or constant NAME, not a
# credential. Re-verify by hand before adding a new line. Never add a broad
# regex/path allowlist here — that would blind the scanner instead of
# dismissing one confirmed false positive.
#
# Fingerprints are relative to the repository root, because the CI job
# mounts the checkout at /workspace and scans `.` from there (see the
# workflow) — an absolute-path fingerprint would not match a GitHub Actions
# runner's checkout path.

# PHP/libsodium constant name (SODIUM_CRYPTO_AEAD_XCHACHA20POLY1305_IETF_KEYBYTES),
# not a secret value. High-entropy match is coincidental to the constant's name.
apps/api/app/Support/Crypto/EnvelopeCipher.php:generic-api-key:43

# Comment naming the OpenBao/Vault transit key algorithm ("chacha20-poly1305"),
# not a key or token value.
docker/openbao/init.sh:generic-api-key:17
